Human Metabolome Database (HMDB 5.0) — 9 media, and 3 further media derived from HMDB tables
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Wishart DS et al. HMDB 5.0: the Human Metabolome Database for 2022. Nucleic Acids Research
2022;50(D1):D622-D631. doi:10.1093/nar/gkab1062
https://hmdb.ca/

  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0)
  "All data and metadata in the HMDB are released under the Creative Commons (CC)
   Attribution-NonCommercial (NC) 4.0 International Licensing condition."

  Evidence caveat, stated rather than hidden: hmdb.ca is Cloudflare-gated and returned HTTP
  403 to every retrieval method attempted on 2026-09-06 (curl with a browser user agent,
  three URL variants). The quote above is from the first-party page as captured by the
  Internet Archive on 2026-01-02:
  https://web.archive.org/web/20260102200014/https://hmdb.ca/about
  It is corroborated by the identical clause on the first-party pages of HMDB's sibling
  databases FooDB and BMDB. Re-verify first-party before relying on it commercially.

  The 3 derived media take their values from HMDB-derived supplementary tables of:
  Ardalani O et al. Rare metabolic gene essentiality is a determinant of microniche
  adaptation in Escherichia coli. PLOS Pathogens 2025. doi:10.1371/journal.ppat.1013775
  That paper is open access, but republication in a CC BY paper does not relicense the
  underlying HMDB values, so these records are labelled NC and flagged for review.


