Primary literature — 1,457 media
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1,369 media curated through GrowthDB (https://github.com/omidard/GrowthDB) and 88 mined from
genome-scale-model papers. Each carries the citation of the publication whose formulation it
encodes, and, where the publication is in PubMed Central, its PMC identifier in
`provenance.primary_identifier`.

  The formulations are facts reported in those publications; the publications themselves are
  not redistributed here. This project asserts CC BY 4.0 over its own compilation, mapping and
  encoding only. Anyone reusing a medium must cite the primary publication.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Classic and standard formulations — 297 media
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Canonical laboratory media (LB, M9, MOPS, M63, BHI, TSB, Davis, and others) encoded to BiGG
exchanges. Each record cites the canonical reference it was formulated from — for example
Bertani G, J Bacteriol 1951;62:293-300 for LB; Sambrook & Russell, Molecular Cloning, CSHL
2001 for M9; Neidhardt FC, Bloch PL, Smith DF, J Bacteriol 1974;119:736-747 for MOPS.

  5 of these records carry a MediaDive URL as their composition link, so their formulation may
  have been taken from a CC BY source requiring attribution and licence indication. They are
  flagged `license_review_required` rather than silently claimed as project-compiled.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Composition that this project generated, not any source
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
229,486 of 665,582 component records (34.5%) were produced by this project's pipeline and are
not stated by the source the record cites. They are retained and labelled, never removed:
`components[].evidence_class` is `sourced` or `derived`, and derived components carry a
`derived_class` of `inferred_from_listed_ingredient` (127,303 — a complex ingredient the
recipe does list, broken down by convention), `injected_convention` (101,796 — a mineral or
gas panel nothing in the recipe corresponds to) or `canonical_base_expansion` (387 — a named
base medium expanded to its published composition).

Standard compositions used for those inferences are credited in each affected record's
`provenance.decomposition_refs`, and include:
  BD Bionutrient Technical Manual, 3rd edition, Becton Dickinson.
  Atlas RM, Handbook of Microbiological Media, 4th edition, CRC Press, 2010.

These components are excluded from the source-coverage figure (`coverage_source`) so that no
medium can report high coverage on composition this project invented.
